From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:20:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Set a growth limit from a zero non-spanning contribution
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

css-grid-2 §12.5 step 2 sets an intrinsic track's growth limit to the
largest min-content or max-content contribution of its span-1 items.
The growth limit was only updated when that contribution was above zero,
so a track that held only an empty item kept an infinite growth limit.
Spanning items then treated it as unlimited and put their extra space
into it instead of into the tracks that the new "distribute space to
non-affected tracks" step should reach.

The final sizes rarely changed, because an infinite growth limit becomes
the base size at the end of the algorithm, but css-grid/grid-model/
grid-gutters-and-flex-content-001.html (WPT ed5a113c) puts a 1px and a
51px overflow into the wrong column.

Upstream Taffy (main) has the same `> 0.0` check.
---
 src/compute/grid/track_sizing.rs | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/compute/grid/track_sizing.rs b/src/compute/grid/track_sizing.rs
index c65bf04..94b017d 100644
--- a/src/compute/grid/track_sizing.rs
+++ b/src/compute/grid/track_sizing.rs
@@ -604,6 +604,11 @@ fn resolve_intrinsic_track_sizes<Tree: LayoutPartialTree>(
         // consider the items in it with a span of 1:
         let batch_span = batch[0].placement(axis).span();
         if !is_flex && batch_span == 1 {
+            // An item's contribution sets its track's growth limit even when it is zero, so start
+            // below any contribution to tell "no item" from "a zero contribution".
+            for track in axis_tracks.iter_mut() {
+                track.growth_limit_planned_increase = f32::NEG_INFINITY;
+            }
             for item in batch.iter_mut() {
                 let track_index = item.placement_indexes(axis).start + 1;
                 let track = &axis_tracks[track_index as usize];
@@ -692,7 +697,7 @@ fn resolve_intrinsic_track_sizes<Tree: LayoutPartialTree>(
             }

             for track in axis_tracks.iter_mut() {
-                if track.growth_limit_planned_increase > 0.0 {
+                if track.growth_limit_planned_increase != f32::NEG_INFINITY {
                     track.growth_limit = if track.growth_limit == f32::INFINITY {
                         track.growth_limit_planned_increase
                     } else {
